BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-20261004-67@tonight
DTSTAMP:20261005T091727Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261004T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261004T210000
SUMMARY:Pedrito Martinez - Show 1
LOCATION:Cafe Wha?\, Greenwich Village
DESCRIPTION:Looking for the 9:30pm show? Click HERE for tickets Grammy-winn
 
ing percussionist Pedrito Martinez makes his debut appearance at Bleecker B
 
ell\, ensuring to thrill the audience with electrifying rhythms\, powerful 
 
vocals\, and infectious energy. Widely regarded as the greatest living Afro
 
-Cuban percussionist\, Martinez has collaborated with artists ranging from 
 
Paul Simon and Bruce Springsteen to Wynton Marsalis. His ensemble transform
 
s every performance into a celebration of dance\, heritage\, and improvisat
 
ion\, turning rhythm into pure joy and making it impossible to sit still. A
 
 Festival favorite\, this is an evening of unforgettable music\, irresistib
 
le grooves\, and singular spontaneity. About Pedrito Martinez Pedrito Marti
 
nez is an internationally acclaimed percussionist\, singer\, and bandleader
 
 widely recognized as one of the leading ambassadors of Afro-Cuban music. R
 
aised in Havana's Cayo Hueso neighborhood\, where rumba is a way of life\, 
 
he developed a deep foundation in Afro-Cuban traditions and their African o
 
rigins. The New York Times has hailed him as \, "rdquo" -> a source of rhyt
 
hmic delight...as close as traditional Afro-Cuban music has to a superstar.
 
" Since settling in New York City\, Martinez has recorded and performed wit
 
h an extraordinary range of artists\, including Paul Simon\, Wynton Marsali
 
s\, Sting\, Bruce Springsteen\, Rubén Blades\, Eric Clapton\, and Camila C
 
abello\, contributing to more than 75 albums. A founding member of the infl
 
uential Afro-Cuban/Afrobeat band Yerba Buena\, he launched The Pedrito Mart
 
inez Group in 2005\, earning Grammy and Latin Grammy nominations. Frequentl
 
y named Jazz Percussionist of the Year in critics' polls\, Martinez continu
 
es to tour worldwide\, celebrated for his virtuosity\, rhythmic power\, and
 
 charismatic stage presence. Tickets & info: https://www.ticketweb.com/even
 
t/pedrito-martinez-show-cafe-wha-tickets/14964153
URL:https://www.ticketweb.com/event/pedrito-martinez-show-cafe-wha-tickets/
 
14964153
END:VEVENT
